  "title": "FDA Suspends NSCI Food Licence and Fines Mumbai University Canteen Over Hygiene Violations",
  "summary": "The Maharashtra Food and Drug Administration (FDA) suspended the food licence of the National Sports Club of India (NSCI) in Mumbai for safety violations, including flies in the main kitchen and cockroaches in the wash basin. A fine of ₹1 lakh was imposed on a Mumbai University canteen at the Fort area for failing to meet hygiene standards. The FDA conducted inspections and found serious breaches under Schedule 4 of the Food Safety and Standards (Licensing and Registration of Food Businesses) Regulations, 2011.",
