      "description": "The Maharashtra Food and Drug Administration (FDA) has said it has suspended the food licence of the National Sports Club of India (NSCI) in Mumbai for safety violations after inspectors found flies in the main kitchen and cockroaches in the wash basin area.\nThe regulator, in a statement on Monday, also said it has imposed a fine of Rs 1 lakh on a canteen at the Mumbai University in the Fort area for contravening food safety norms.\nThe FDA said it conducted inspections of the NSCI and found breaches of hygiene and sanitary provisions in its premises.\n\"M/s The National Sports Club of India, Worli, Mumbai was inspected. Serious violations of hygiene and sanitary provisions under Schedule 4 of the Food Safety and Standards (Licensing and Registration of Food Businesses) Regulations, 2011 were found. The food licence of the establishment has been suspended with immediate effect on November 23,\" the statement said.\nListing the reasons for licence suspension, the FDA said flies were foun",
